+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) support for PCRE2 10.49 (upstream plus MSYS2 patches), on branch `arm64-port`.
+
+PCRE2 is portable C, and the bundled sljit JIT already has an ARM64 backend that `sljitConfigCPU.h:157` selects for `_M_ARM64`. The CMake build needed no changes for ARM64. The port is one source-line change, which re-enables the ARM64 JIT SIMD fast paths when the compiler is MSVC.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- None. `CMakeLists.txt` has no architecture checks. The `-mshstk` probe is gated on `__CET__`, which is x86-only. The MSVC settings don't depend on the architecture. `cmake -A ARM64` works unchanged.
+
+### Source Code
+- `src/pcre2_jit_simd_inc.h:767` adds `|| defined _M_ARM64` to the gate for the ARM64 JIT SIMD block.
+  - cl.exe targeting ARM64 does not predefine `__ARM_NEON`/`__ARM_NEON__`. This was checked with `cl -EP` on MSVC 14.51.
+  - Without the change, MSVC builds silently compiled out `JIT_HAS_FAST_FORWARD_CHAR_SIMD`, `JIT_HAS_FAST_REQUESTED_CHAR_SIMD` and `JIT_HAS_FAST_FORWARD_CHAR_PAIR_SIMD`.
+  - The block emits A64 AdvSIMD through sljit and uses no C intrinsics. AdvSIMD is mandatory on Windows ARM64.
+  - GCC and Clang behave exactly as before.
+
+### CI/CD
+- None. The repository has no CI configuration.
+
+### New Files
+- This file only.
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- Visual Studio 2022 or later with the **MSVC ARM64 build tools** and a **Windows 11 SDK**. This port was built with VS 18.8 and MSVC 14.51.36231.
+- CMake 3.15 or later. The copy bundled with VS works.
+
+### Build
+```powershell
+cmake -S . -B build-arm64 -G "Visual Studio 18 2026" -A ARM64 `
+  -DPCRE2_SUPPORT_JIT=ON -DPCRE2_BUILD_TESTS=ON `
+  -DPCRE2_BUILD_PCRE2_8=ON -DPCRE2_BUILD_PCRE2_16=ON -DPCRE2_BUILD_PCRE2_32=ON `
+  -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
+cmake --build build-arm64 --config Release --parallel
+```
+- Use `-G "Visual Studio 17 2022"` with VS 2022.
+- Build output goes to `build-arm64\Release`.
+- The build produced 0 warnings and 0 errors.
+
+### Run Tests
+Run from cmd or PowerShell, not an MSYS shell:
+```powershell
+ctest --test-dir build-arm64 -C Release --output-on-failure
+build-arm64\Release\pcre2test.exe -C     # expect "Architecture: ARM-64 64bit (little endian + unaligned)"
+```
+Expected result: 4 passed, 0 failed.
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+PCRE2 has no benchmark suite, so no benchmark file was produced.
+
